  "observations": [
    "Inspected all six unobstructed authored-meter population screenshots: 1, 20 and 100 copies, each as clones and as explicit InstancedMesh groups. Crown contact is on the reference plane, plant proportions/materials remain consistent, and spatially separated repeated plants retain their layered form. No errors are reported.",
    "Typical 20-copy clones submit 62 calls/154,722 triangles; explicit instancing submits 5 calls/154,722 triangles. Stress 100-copy clones submit 302 calls/773,602 triangles; instancing submits 5 calls/773,602 triangles. Counts include two reference drawables and two floor triangles; one fern remains 3 primitives/7,736 triangles.",
    "Instancing reduces draw submissions but does not reduce triangle count. Clone/instanced screenshots use the same population camera and source data; their nearly matching pixels support representation consistency. The catalogue viewer does not thereby gain automatic population instancing.",
    "Each population records 20 synchronous render/finish samples under Chromium 141 ANGLE SwiftShader WebGL2 at 1600×1000. These measurements establish workload and correctness in this software context only. No physical device or frame-time target was supplied, so repeated-groundcover device performance remains unknown and is not an approval claim."
  ],
